// Hand-written. farming.constant is generated by tools/farming/gen.py, so anything added there is
// lost on the next regeneration; these are not part of the crop table and live here.

// AUTOWEED. Past this Farming level, empty patches stop going back to weeds and any weeds already
// on one are gone the next time the patch is looked at - see ~farming_regrow_weeds in
// farming_core.rs2.
//
// 65 is Corey's own number ("could lock it behind a lvl/xp req like 65 or 70 farming"). There is
// nothing to copy it from: auto-weeding is an RS3 feature, not an Old School one, so this is a
// chosen number rather than a sourced one. 65 is also where the Farming Guild's middle tier opens
// in Old School, which is the closest thing to a precedent there is.
^farming_autoweed_level = 65
